Build the platform so it gives better real-time answers, using realistic mock data that is structured so live APIs can be plugged in later. This means live weather and seasonal conditions for each destination and date, price-drop alerts with a small "Price just dropped" badge, an automatic check at booking that confirms visa requirements, passport validity and layover length before the user pays, and a visible "all-in price" toggle that is on by default. Add an AI trip assistant in a floating chat bubble that answers real questions in plain language, such as "Is it safe to travel here alone in March?" or "Do I need a visa?", and responds with short, direct answers rather than long paragraphs. The booking flow should be a single clean page with a progress bar, minimal form fields, saved traveller details, and clear confirmation messaging.

Trip dashboard, groups and footer

Include a simple trip dashboard after booking where the user sees their itinerary, a refund and cancellation tracker with a clear status, and a one-tap "I have a problem" button that opens help for issues like delays, lost bookings or changes. Add a group trip feature that lets friends or family share one itinerary, vote on options and split costs, plus an optional "Travellers on this trip" section where users can choose to share itineraries and meet other travellers, always with privacy controls and safety verification. The footer should be near-black with white text and a blue call-to-action. Keep all microcopy warm, short and jargon-free, for example "Here's what we'd pick for you" instead of "Search results". Every page must be fully responsive, fast-loading, and designed so a first-time user can go from landing to booking in under two minutes without feeling lost.
